# K3 Cognitive Runtime

SecureSkills router/amplifier — **never** a topical veto. Full detail: skill `k3-cognitive-router` → `references/full-runtime.md`.

## Fast path (default)

Use for Q&A, small edits, status, and normal Composer Fast turns — unless the user asks for depth/orchestration or full-spectrum triggers (`máximo provecho`, `libertad total`, `usa todo el stack`, hard multi-domain):

- **Reply first** — minimal preamble; do not narrate RAOVA or routing in the answer
- `effort: low` · Top-k **0–2** · **no** Task subagents · **no** `.k3/` · **no** GRM · **no** L2 grep
- **Batch tools in parallel** when independent; prefer one Act round when sufficient
- **Semgrep/SAST after** code edits when available — do not delay the first helpful reply on non-code questions
- Escalate to `high`/`max`, subagents, L2, or `.k3/` only when clearly multi-step, audit-grade, or user-requested

## Full-spectrum (on trigger)

Any topic · effort `max` · Top-k up to **16** · harness `full-spectrum` · wave experts · GRM optional · cyber/ruflo/SPARC/MCP eligible

## Deep work only

RAOVA, preserved thinking, partial rollout, L1→L2 (`grep` one shard line → one `SKILL.md`, max 4/task, never whole shard) — see `catalog-l2.md`

